<title>FINLAND: FINNISH CO-OP BANKS TO CUT OP-PRIME RATE TO 4.75%.</title>
<headline>FINNISH CO-OP BANKS TO CUT OP-PRIME RATE TO 4.75%.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish cooperative banking group said in a statement on Tuesday its OP-Prime reference rate would be lowered to 4.75 percent from 5.00 percent effective October 1.  </p>
<p>&quot;The lowering of the interest rate is based on the fall in market interest rates and moderate inflation expectations,&quot; OKOBANK said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
